  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life-Saving, Multi-Sectoral Emergency Assistance and Protection to Vulnerable Displaced Persons in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia has one of the most complex human mobility environments in the world, with factors ranging from conflict, drought, environmental degradation, to changing livelihood strategies. The prolonged drought is affecting 24.1 million people living in drought-affected areas in Ethiopia, mainly in southern and south-eastern areas of Oromia, Southern Nations Nationalities and People (SNNP), Southwest and Somali regions. The objective of this action is to contribute to preventing, reducing, and mitigating protection threats for persons affected by crisis in Ethiopia through the provision of multi-sector lifesaving humanitarian assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
